    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d632">

                <pb facs="0774" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg678"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 52.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 53, of the 21st of December last, reporting that you have protested
                    to the Siamese Government against the action of Siamese officials in seizing
                    property belonging to Messrs. Bartine Carrington and. J. B. West, American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>The Department approves generally your action as reported in your dispatch.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
